# C — finance by fiscal year (1 July to 30 June), USD, accrual (US GAAP). The two latest years are the audited consolidated statements (the Foundation and
# Wikimedia, LLC); earlier years are ProPublica's extraction of each Form 990, which classifies a little differently (2024-25: audited revenue $208.6M,
# Form 990 $205.4M). "net-income" is the increase in net assets; "operating-expenses" is total expenses. Plans are budgets, not results.
# The period id is the accounting reader's own (2024-07..2025-06), so a later books export lands on the same node.
nodes:
  - id: C:finance/2024-07-to-2025-06
    type: finance
    name: FY2024-25 (July 2024 to June 2025), audited
    summary: Revenue $208.6M, expenses $190.9M (77.4% programs, 11.4% fundraising, 11.2% administration), net assets $296.6M, about 17 months of expenses; contributions $184.1M, Wikimedia Enterprise $8.3M, awards and grants $28.7M.
    by: atom/wikimedia-foundation
    period: 2024-07..2025-06
    currency: USD
    basis: accrual
    figures: {revenue: 208567153, operating-expenses: 190938007, net-income: 24994640, cash: 72028717, assets: 310794417, liabilities: 14244387, equity: 296550030}
    detail: {contributions-of-cash-and-financial-assets: 184053816, enterprise-revenue: 8297917, investment-income: 6862192, awards-and-grants: 28737437, salaries-and-benefits: 114039077, internet-hosting: 3474785, donation-processing: 8252081, investments-fair-value: 213347452, net-assets-with-donor-restrictions: 3815000}
    form-990: {revenue: 205389744, expenses: 189748442, net-assets: 296550030, total-assets: 310794417}
    consolidates: []
    status: active
    visibility: public
    owner: O:role/chief-financial-officer
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ["https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/foundation/3/3f/Wikimedia_Foundation_FY_24-25_Audit_Report.pdf", "https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Wikimedia_Foundation_reports/Financial/Audits/2024-2025_-_frequently_asked_questions", "https://wikimediafoundation.org/about/annualreport/2024-2025-annual-report/", "https://projects.propublica.org/nonprofits/organizations/200049703"], confidence: 0.9, state: known}

